<title>NEW ZEALAND: Tax cuts after 1998 not possible under NZS -Peters.</title>
<headline>Tax cuts after 1998 not possible under NZS -Peters.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Treasurer Winston Peters said on Wednesday tax cuts beyond next year would not be possible if the current universal pension scheme was retained because the money would be needed to fund retirement incomes.</p>
<p>&quot;Under NZS (New Zealand Superannuation -- the current scheme) those tax cuts would not be possible, because the taxes would be needed to fund the retirement incomes of future generations,&quot; Peters said in a speech to the New Plymouth Chamber of Commerce.</p>
</text>
